---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Work — Jędrzej Szymula"
  description="SEO case studies by Jędrzej Szymula — real projects, real results."
  path="/work.html"
  active="work"
  ogTitle="Work — Jędrzej Szymula, SEO Specialist"
  ogDescription="SEO case studies: healthcare RCM, fintech, IT and e-commerce — content, branding, and SEO / AEO / GEO with measurable results."
>

  <div class="section-label">Case Studies</div>

  <!-- Case Study — Flobotics -->
  <div class="case" id="flobotics" onclick="toggle(this)">
    <div class="case-header">
      <span class="case-title">Flobotics</span>
      <span class="case-meta">Healthcare RCM · Content · 2025–now</span>
    </div>
    <p class="case-desc">Supported Flobotics' rebrand and pivot towards U.S. healthcare revenue cycle management — driving market visibility through content strategy, LinkedIn personal branding, brand positioning, and SEO / AEO / GEO.</p>
    <div class="stats">
      <div><span class="stat-value">2×</span><span class="stat-label">U.S. blog growth YoY</span></div>
      <div><span class="stat-value">100K+</span><span class="stat-label">LinkedIn reach</span></div>
      <div><span class="stat-value">40</span><span class="stat-label">AI citations</span></div>
      <div><span class="stat-value">96%</span><span class="stat-label">Ahrefs score</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tags">
      <span class="tag">Rebranding</span>
      <span class="tag">Content Strategy</span>
      <span class="tag">LinkedIn</span>
      <span class="tag">SEO / AEO / GEO</span>
      <span class="tag">Healthcare RCM</span>
    </div>
    <p class="toggle-hint">Click to read more ↓</p>
    <div class="case-body">
      <p><strong>Context.</strong> Flobotics, an automation company, rebranded and pivoted towards U.S. healthcare revenue cycle management (RCM). The new positioning needed market visibility, credibility, and recognition in a niche where trust decides who gets shortlisted.</p>
      <p><strong>My role.</strong> I supported the rebrand and the pivot end to end: content creation and strategy, personal brand development on LinkedIn, brand positioning and recognition, and SEO / AEO / GEO — making the brand findable both in search and in AI answers.</p>
      <!-- Featured report — PDF in /downloads, previews in /images -->
      <section class="report" aria-labelledby="flo-report-title">
        <p class="report-kicker">Featured piece · Market report</p>
        <div class="report-grid">
          <figure class="report-cover">
            <img src="images/flobotics-rcm-2026-cover.jpg" alt="Cover of the Flobotics report State of RCM Automation: 2026 Edition" width="900" height="1165" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>Cover · 15 pages · CC BY 4.0</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="report-body">
            <h3 class="report-title" id="flo-report-title">State of RCM Automation: 2026 Edition</h3>
            <p>A review of what changed for U.S. hospital and health-system revenue cycles in 2026 — legal &amp; regulatory moves, finance &amp; payments shifts, and new AI tools — quarter by quarter, with commentary from four Flobotics leaders and four bets for 2027. Every figure carries an evidence grade and a numbered source.</p>
            <div class="stats">
              <div><span class="stat-value">15</span><span class="stat-label">Pages</span></div>
              <div><span class="stat-value">61</span><span class="stat-label">Sources</span></div>
              <div><span class="stat-value">4</span><span class="stat-label">Experts</span></div>
              <div><span class="stat-value">3</span><span class="stat-label">Fact-checks</span></div>
            </div>
            <dl class="results results-list report-contrib">
              <div class="results-group">
                <dt>My contribution</dt>
                <dd>Compiled the report (credited as “Compiled by”) and planned its structure: a 4-point summary, a quarter-by-quarter timeline of 2026, expert commentary, and predictions for 2027.</dd>
                <dd>Research and fact-checking against primary records wherever they exist — CMS, the Federal Register, DOJ, HHS-OIG, court opinions, company filings — with sponsored content excluded.</dd>
                <dd>An evidence-grade system for all 61 sources, so readers see at a glance what is a primary record and what is opinion.</dd>
                <dd>Shaped the commentary of the CEO, CTO, CDO and Lead AI &amp; Automation Advisor into data-backed sections.</dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
            <p class="grades" aria-label="Evidence grades used in the report">
              <span class="grade"><b>P</b> primary record</span>
              <span class="grade"><b>I</b> independent survey</span>
              <span class="grade"><b>V</b> vendor-funded</span>
              <span class="grade"><b>S</b> secondary</span>
              <span class="grade"><b>E</b> opinion / forecast</span>
            </p>
            <a href="downloads/flobotics-state-of-rcm-automation-2026.pdf" class="btn" download>Download the report (PDF, 1.2 MB)</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="report-pages">
          <figure>
            <img src="images/flobotics-rcm-2026-p2.jpg" alt="Page 2 of the report: summary in four points" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>p. 2 · Report summary</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img src="images/flobotics-rcm-2026-p12.jpg" alt="Page 12 of the report: method and evidence grades" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>p. 12 · Method &amp; evidence grades</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>

      <dl class="results">
        <div class="results-group">
          <dt>Content</dt>
          <dd>2× year-on-year growth of the blog in the U.S.</dd>
          <dd>100+ articles across 5 categories — AI, RCM, RPA, EHR, Healthcare</dd>
          <dd>20+ case studies, written or curated around traced results and internal interviews</dd>
          <dd>30+ niche-specific glossary terms</dd>
          <dd>40+ FAQ pieces</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="results-group">
          <dt>Social media</dt>
          <dd>4 defined expert voices (CEO, CDO, CTO, CIO) across all channels</dd>
          <dd>50+ LinkedIn posts</dd>
          <dd>100K+ members reached — one post alone hit 16K impressions within a week</dd>
          <dd>500+ engagements</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="results-group">
          <dt>Branding</dt>
          <dd>Cooperation with 3 external marketing agencies, including results verification — ICP identification, UX writing, messaging, GTM strategy, ABM copy</dd>
          <dd>5 trust touchpoints: Clutch, Crunchbase, GoodFirms, G2, Capterra</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="results-group">
          <dt>Optimisation</dt>
          <dd>96% Ahrefs health score</dd>
          <dd>JSON-LD structured data and an llms.txt file</dd>
          <dd>40 AI citations &amp; AI Overview appearances within 3 months</dd>
          <dd>2 migrations: WordPress → Webflow, then Webflow → a custom Astro site built with AI assistance and deployed from GitHub</dd>
          <dd>A library of trusted sources built from handpicked, up-to-date industry reports</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Case Study — mobility.autopay.eu -->
  <div class="case" id="autopay" onclick="toggle(this)">
    <div class="case-header">
      <span class="case-title">mobility.autopay.eu</span>
      <span class="case-meta">Fintech · Content · 2024–2026</span>
    </div>
    <p class="case-desc">Built a content engine from the ground up for Autopay — one of Poland's leading fintech and mobility payment platforms — following a domain takeover. Led a team of copywriters to produce ~1,000 expert articles in under 12 months.</p>
    <div class="stats">
      <div><span class="stat-value">4.89M</span><span class="stat-label">GSC impressions</span></div>
      <div><span class="stat-value">38.2K</span><span class="stat-label">Organic clicks</span></div>
      <div><span class="stat-value">~1,000</span><span class="stat-label">Articles published</span></div>
      <div><span class="stat-value">12mo</span><span class="stat-label">Timeline</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tags">
      <span class="tag">Content Strategy</span>
      <span class="tag">Content Management</span>
      <span class="tag">Team Lead</span>
      <span class="tag">Internal Linking</span>
      <span class="tag">Fintech</span>
    </div>
    <p class="toggle-hint">Click to read more ↓</p>
    <div class="case-body">
      <p><strong>Context.</strong> Autopay is a major player in the Polish fintech and mobility payments market. Following a domain takeover, the team needed to build SEO authority and organic visibility from scratch — quickly and at scale. I was brought in based on a working relationship built through a prior project (winiety-online.pl) throughout 2024.</p>
      <p><strong>My role.</strong> As Content Team Lead at Mamalu.io (Jul 2024 – Oct 2026), on the Autopay Vignettes project, working closely with 3 co-founders, I took full ownership of the content strategy: defining topic clusters, keyword architecture, and internal linking logic. As content manager I recruited and managed a team of 2 specialist copywriters, set editorial standards, and oversaw quality across every article produced.</p>
      <p><strong>What we built.</strong> Close to 1,000 expert, in-depth articles covering mobility, payments, and fintech topics — each mapped to a specific search intent and connected through a deliberate internal linking structure. Most site copy was also crafted or shaped by the team.</p>
      <p><strong>Results.</strong> Within 12 months the site reached 4.89 million impressions and 38,200 clicks in Google Search Console, with a clear exponential growth trajectory beginning in Q4 2025 and accelerating into 2026. Average position 9.9 across the full keyword footprint — with significant upside still ahead as authority compounds.</p>
      <figure class="shot">
        <img src="images/screen-mobilityautopayeu-1.png" alt="Google Search Console — total clicks and impressions for mobility.autopay.eu" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Google Search Console · Total clicks &amp; impressions · Apr 2025 – Mar 2026</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="shot">
        <img src="images/screen-mobilityautopayeu-6.png" alt="Ahrefs — Domain Rating vs organic traffic for mobility.autopay.eu" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Ahrefs · Domain Rating vs Organic Traffic · Apr 2025 – Apr 2026</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Case Study — Milo Solutions -->
  <div class="case" id="milo-solutions" onclick="toggle(this)">
    <div class="case-header">
      <span class="case-title">Milo Solutions</span>
      <span class="case-meta">IT &amp; Web3 · Content &amp; SEO · 2024–2025</span>
    </div>
    <p class="case-desc">Launched a new company blog from scratch and grew it to 1,800+ daily visits within three months, with 60+ English-language pieces for the IT industry, plus an educational Web3 blog.</p>
    <div class="stats">
      <div><span class="stat-value">1,800+</span><span class="stat-label">Daily visits</span></div>
      <div><span class="stat-value">3mo</span><span class="stat-label">To get there</span></div>
      <div><span class="stat-value">60+</span><span class="stat-label">IT content pieces</span></div>
      <div><span class="stat-value">0 → 1</span><span class="stat-label">Blog built from scratch</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tags">
      <span class="tag">SEO</span>
      <span class="tag">Content Strategy</span>
      <span class="tag">B2B IT</span>
      <span class="tag">Web3</span>
      <span class="tag">Research</span>
    </div>
    <p class="toggle-hint">Click to read more ↓</p>
    <div class="case-body">
      <p><strong>Context.</strong> Milo Solutions needed an organic channel in English to reach international IT buyers — starting with no blog at all.</p>
      <p><strong>My role.</strong> I joined as a freelance Digital Marketing Specialist (Jan – Jul 2024) to build the blog from the ground up, then stayed on full-time as Research &amp; Content Specialist (Jul 2024 – Jun 2025).</p>
      <p><strong>What we built.</strong> 60+ pieces of IT content in English — technical articles and client case studies — plus an educational blog about Web3, backed by a long list of on-site SEO improvements.</p>
      <p><strong>Results.</strong> The new blog went from zero to 1,800+ visits a day within three months.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Case Study — winiety-online.pl -->
  <div class="case" id="winiety-online" onclick="toggle(this)">
    <div class="case-header">
      <span class="case-title">winiety-online.pl</span>
      <span class="case-meta">E-commerce · SEO · 2023–2024</span>
    </div>
    <p class="case-desc">Grew organic visibility for a Polish e-commerce platform in the competitive toll vignette market, reaching top competitive position by traffic value and establishing the working relationship that led to the Autopay project.</p>
    <div class="stats">
      <div><span class="stat-value">1,000+</span><span class="stat-label">TOP 3 keywords</span></div>
      <div><span class="stat-value">+250%</span><span class="stat-label">Visibility</span></div>
      <div><span class="stat-value">$125K+</span><span class="stat-label">Sales from content</span></div>
      <div><span class="stat-value">140K</span><span class="stat-label">Peak visits / mo</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tags">
      <span class="tag">E-commerce SEO</span>
      <span class="tag">Content Strategy</span>
      <span class="tag">Keyword Research</span>
      <span class="tag">Poland</span>
    </div>
    <p class="toggle-hint">Click to read more ↓</p>
    <div class="case-body">
      <p><strong>Context.</strong> winiety-online.pl operates in the Polish toll vignette market — a highly seasonal, competitive niche with well-established players. The goal was to grow organic market share and establish the site as the dominant content authority in the space.</p>
      <p><strong>My role.</strong> Senior Content Writer at Mamalu.io (freelance, Nov 2023 – Jul 2024), responsible for content and SEO on winiety-online.pl.</p>
      <p><strong>Approach.</strong> Developed and executed a content and keyword strategy targeting the full range of vignette-related searches across European markets. Built topical depth to establish authority and supported with a structured internal linking framework.</p>
      <p><strong>Results.</strong> 1,000+ keywords moved into Google’s TOP 3, visibility in Google grew by 250%, and the content drove purchases worth over $125,000. The site reached 140K monthly organic visits at peak (Domain Rating 55), with organic traffic value exceeding $10K/month — placing it clearly ahead of all major organic competitors in the Polish market by both traffic volume and value. This project directly led to the Autopay engagement in 2024.</p>
      <figure class="shot">
        <img src="images/screen-mobilityautopayeu-3.png" alt="Ahrefs — top organic competitors, winiety-online.pl leading by traffic value" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Ahrefs · Top organic competitors · winiety-online.pl dominant by traffic value</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="shot">
        <img src="images/screen-mobilityautopayeu-4.png" alt="Ahrefs — Domain Rating vs organic traffic, long-term growth for winiety-online.pl" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Ahrefs · Domain Rating vs Organic Traffic · long-term growth view</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-label section-label--spaced">Earlier Work</div>

  <dl class="results results-list">
    <div class="results-group">
      <dt>BimmerTech <span class="dt-meta">Technical Copywriter · 2022–2023</span></dt>
      <dd>Technical and expert articles in English for an international audience on the BimmerTech blog.</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="results-group">
      <dt>Rightout <span class="dt-meta">UX Writer · 2023</span></dt>
      <dd>All copy for an IT-outsourcing portal — the landing page and the rest of the site, from button labels to marketing headlines and the FAQ.</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="results-group">
      <dt>Finelf.com <span class="dt-meta">Copy / SEO Editor · 2022</span></dt>
      <dd>Expert articles, editing, and online publishing for czerwona-skarbonka.pl.</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="results-group">
      <dt>Fintek.pl <span class="dt-meta">Web Editor · 2022</span></dt>
      <dd>Tech and finance news, breakdowns of new legislation, and technical articles.</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="results-group">
      <dt>Freelance <span class="dt-meta">Copywriter · 2021</span></dt>
      <dd>Copywriting and SEO engagements for a range of clients.</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="results-group">
      <dt>Profisun Polska <span class="dt-meta">Junior Brand Manager · 2020</span></dt>
      <dd>Visual identity and graphic materials for the consortium, SEO optimisation in WordPress, and social media management in Hootsuite.</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>

  <div class="section-label section-label--spaced">Free Resources</div>

  <article class="product">
    <div class="product-header">
      <span class="product-title">On-Page SEO Checklist</span>
      <span class="product-price">Free</span>
    </div>
    <p class="product-desc">
      The exact checklist used to audit titles, headings, internal linking, and content structure before a page ships.
    </p>
    <ul class="includes">
      <li>Title, meta, and heading structure rules</li>
      <li>Internal linking &amp; content depth checks</li>
      <li>Image, URL, and schema basics</li>
    </ul>
    <a href="downloads/on-page-seo-checklist.pdf" class="btn" download>Download PDF</a>
  </article>

  <article class="product">
    <div class="product-header">
      <span class="product-title">Off-Page SEO Checklist</span>
      <span class="product-price">Free</span>
    </div>
    <p class="product-desc">
      A field-tested framework for building authority safely — link quality, outreach, and brand signals.
    </p>
    <ul class="includes">
      <li>Link quality &amp; relevance criteria</li>
      <li>Outreach and digital PR angles that work</li>
      <li>Brand mention &amp; authority signals to track</li>
    </ul>
    <a href="downloads/off-page-seo-checklist.pdf" class="btn" download>Download PDF</a>
  </article>

  <article class="product">
    <div class="product-header">
      <span class="product-title">Technical SEO Checklist</span>
      <span class="product-price">Free</span>
    </div>
    <p class="product-desc">
      A quick pass for the technical foundations that quietly decide whether the rest of your SEO work compounds.
    </p>
    <ul class="includes">
      <li>Crawlability, indexation &amp; sitemap checks</li>
      <li>Core Web Vitals &amp; page speed basics</li>
      <li>Redirects, canonicals &amp; duplicate content</li>
    </ul>
    <a href="downloads/technical-seo-checklist.pdf" class="btn" download>Download PDF</a>
  </article>

  <Fragment slot="scripts">
  <script is:inline>
  function toggle(el){
    if (window.event && window.event.target.closest('a, button, .case-body')) return;
    const body = el.querySelector('.case-body');
    const hint = el.querySelector('.toggle-hint');
    const open = body.classList.toggle('open');
    if(hint) hint.textContent = open ? 'Click to collapse ↑' : 'Click to read more ↓';
  }
</script>
  </Fragment>
</Base>
